I've been playing nethack for a while on a unix system, and there is
something I've been wanting to do for a while but haven't succeeded in
yet. In trying to get good stats/inventory for a particular character,
I've wanted to write a program in which the computer would (for
example) start up a game of nethack for me, do an inventory, and then
save itself. Something like: nethack < commandfile > outputfile, and
then examining 'outputfile' for particular items, etc. (In the above
case, the file commandfile would contain a line of commands like:
nwiSy - to play a Wizard, take inventory, and save the game) The
problem is, whenever I try to have nethack redirect input, I always
get the error message:

NetHack (settty): Not a typewriter
You must play from a terminal.

So my question is, is there a way to get nethack to play from an input
file (or based on the influence of some input program), or else fool
the program into thinking that I'm playing from a terminal? Has anybody
else out there tried to or succeeded in doing something similar?

